## Examples

### Basic
<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.funnel(
    steps=["catalog", "product_view", "add_to_cart", "purchase"],
)`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/funnel/basic.html" height={480} />

### Diff mode
<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.funnel(
    steps=["catalog", "product_view", "add_to_cart", "purchase"],
    diff=["platform", "mobile", "desktop"]
)`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/funnel/diff.html" height={480} />

This descriptive diff splits events: `platform` changes within some users'
paths, so those users appear in both groups. That is why the same `diff` with
`ci_level` raises — intervals need every path in exactly one group.

### Confidence intervals

The demo dataset has no experiment, so this example compares two acquisition
cohorts, `user_cohort`, a segment that is constant per user, on the same
purchase steps as the other examples. The cohorts were not randomised, so the
intervals measure sampling noise, not a causal effect.

<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.funnel(
    steps=["catalog", "product_view", "add_to_cart", "purchase"],
    diff=["user_cohort", "2024-01", "2024-04"],
    ci_level=0.95,
    correction="holm",
)`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/funnel/ci.html" height={640} />
{% endblock %}
